# Gravespeaker three-screen UI + CSS motion

## Context
- Current `src/routes/+page.svelte` is an unstyled single-column form (system-ui, grey borders).
- The all-hallows worktree lives on a cloud session path that isn't on this machine; branch `design/all-hallows` has no UI commits. Mock image is the source of truth; palette is sampled from `Claude outputs/*.png`.
- Goal: Invitation → Searching → Story screens per the mock, CSS-only motion, voice as placeholders. No new features, no animation libraries, no new deps.

## Decisions (settled)
- Palette sampled from screenshots, dark only. Tokens on `:root` in one global stylesheet:
  `--ink` (#0b0d12-ish bg), `--slate` (card), `--bone` (text), `--verdigris` (accent/CTA), `--mist` (muted text/hairlines). Exact hex picked by sampling during step 1.
- Fonts via Google Fonts `<link>` (no package.json change): uncial display caps for wordmark/buttons/labels (Uncial Antiqua — confirm visually against mock, swap if off), IM Fell English (+ italic) for names, tagline, story text; system sans for small UI copy.
- Hero: left crop of `gravespeaker.jpg` (stone + fog + leaves) → `static/invitation.webp`.
- Progress checklist uses real phases only; each step ticks when its request resolves. No timers.
- Header share icon omitted (not an MVP feature). Back arrow = existing `reset()`.

## Structure (one responsibility per file)
- `src/routes/+page.svelte` — keeps all existing state/fetch logic (`call`, `read`, `research`, `tell`, `fail`, `reset`, `showEpitaph`) unchanged; adds `photoUrl` (`URL.createObjectURL`, revoked in `reset`) and maps `phase` → screen. Markup shrinks to choosing a screen component.
- `src/app.css` (imported in `+layout.svelte`) — tokens, fonts, base body, focus ring, `.visually-hidden`, `prefers-reduced-motion` kill switch.
- `src/lib/components/AppHeader.svelte` — back arrow + small wordmark (screens 2–3).
- `src/lib/components/Stepper.svelte` — Photo / Searching / Story, `aria-current="step"`.
- `src/lib/components/Invitation.svelte` — hero backdrop, moon glyph, wordmark, tagline, `Photograph a headstone` file-input label (camera icon, inline SVG), `How it works` `<details>` with the existing explainer copy + "Photos are read in memory…", error/retry slot.
- `src/lib/components/Searching.svelte` — photo frame with scan light, checklist (Reading the stone / Searching historical records / Confirm the match / Building the story) with done/active/pending icons, and the existing `pick` ("Whose story?") and `confirm` ("Is this them?", confidence, source links, "This is them", "None of these") content rendered under the checklist. Footer quote + moon divider.
- `src/lib/components/StoryView.svelte` — name/dates header card, section nav (Story · Facts · Sources as anchor links, all content visible as in the mock), `Story generated with AI` label + one-line "AI reconstruction from the linked records, not testimony", `.paragraph` with left rule, Key facts box (Born/Died from the confirmed candidate only; missing → "unknown"; no place field exists so none shown), Sources list, `Try another photo`. Epitaph outcome reuses the header + Key facts with `epitaph()` lines, the note, and no AI label.
- `src/lib/components/NarrationBar.svelte` — placeholder: fixed bottom bar, disabled play button, disabled voice chip (Male/Female), "Narration coming soon". Only on a told story.

## Motion (CSS only, all disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`)
- Invitation: two fog layers (blurred radial gradients) with slow `translateX` drift, 40–60s alternate; lantern glow = radial gradient with irregular `@keyframes` opacity/scale flicker.
- Searching: `::after` gradient band sweeping `translateY` over the photo while a request is in flight; active step spinner dots pulse; step icon crossfades on done.
- Story: paragraph reveal via `mask-image` gradient wipe + slight `translateY` fade (~1.2s); facts/sources fade in staggered.

## Copy/selector contract kept (e2e depends on it)
- "Photograph a headstone", `input[type=file]` (still focused on load), "Whose story?", "Is this them?", `aria-label="Read from the stone"` (on the Searching inscription summary), confidence strings, "This is them", "None of these", "Story generated with AI", `.paragraph`, "Try again", "Try another photo", `role=alert` errors, epitaph notes.

## Tests
- `src/routes/journey.e2e.ts`: fix any selector the layout moves; add
  - checklist reflects real phases: after read resolves "Reading the stone" is done and research is active (assert via `aria-` state, mocked delayed route).
  - uploaded photo preview shows on the Searching screen.
  - narration control is present and disabled on a told story; absent on epitaph.
- No unit tests for markup/CSS (banned: rendering-only).

## Verification
1. `make ai-checks` (format, lint, svelte-check, vitest, build) — zero warnings.
2. `pnpm test:e2e`.
3. `pnpm preview` + chrome-devtools MCP at 390×844: screenshot all three screens + epitaph, compare to mock; check reduced-motion emulation stops animation; `lighthouse_audit` for a11y/contrast.
4. Semgrep + Sonar scan on the diff if integrations respond.


